Project ENTAIL

Economic Non-Transferable Attestation & Immutable Ledger

Project ENTAIL is the public-facing initiative of the SOS69069 protocol.

The name is intentionally meaningful. "Entail" is an English verb meaning to involve or necessitate as a consequence. This reflects the philosophy of the protocol:

Supporting Ukraine entails creating an immutable public record of participation.

Recording history entails accountability.

Accountability entails sovereignty.

Sovereignty entails long-term resilience.


The acronym captures the protocol's core principles:

Economic — focused on long-term economic coordination rather than speculation.

Non-Transferable — participation rights remain bound to their rightful holder.

Attestation — verified actions are cryptographically recorded.

Immutable Ledger — every participation event becomes a permanent public record.


Project ENTAIL provides a memorable, internationally recognisable identity while expressing the protocol's broader mission: transforming blockchain from a transfer network into infrastructure for immutable participation, economic sovereignty, and resilient national coordination.


